  "worked_solution": "We say that an implication has a *trivial proof* if the consequent is always true:\n\n$$\nP\\,\u21d2\\overset{\\text{Always true}}{\\overset{\u23de}{Q}}\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the antecedent is true or false. \n\nWith that in mind, we proceed as follows:\n\nThe theorem can be written as the implication \n\n$$\nn\\text{\u00a0is even}\\,\u21d2\\,|n|>-1.\n$$\n\nNow, since $|n|$ is non-negative for all $n\\in Z,$ we have the following fact:\n\nThe consequent $|n|>-1$ of our implication is always true.\n\nFinally, we can make the following conclusion:\n\nTherefore, the theorem is trivially true.",
